play out yet, or maybe you know, depending
when you're watching this, but I don't right

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:46.840
now, so yeah.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:52.390
I doubt this will be the case, but the end
to this fight might be really bad, or Kaido

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:55.840
might not have gotten the flashback he deserves.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:02.680
But with all that boring pre-talk out of the
way, what makes this clash more impactful

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:05.920
than Will smith's hand during the oscars?

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:11.580
There are of course a number of things I have
to talk about when it comes to a manga fight.

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:16.190
The battle choreography and art, the set-up
for the fight, the motivation for this fight

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:23.420
and what is at stake, how the characters change
and what the impact is on the overall storyline

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:24.420
at large.

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:26.540
In other words, a lot.

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:27.700
Gosh, so much pre-amble.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:29.140
Let's get on with it.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:30.140
So, set-up.

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:34.790
I hope no-one disagrees with the idea that
this fight between Kaido and Luffy is the

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:37.360
climax of the Wano arc.

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:43.010
Which is not only the longest arc in the history
of manga, I assume, I actually don't know,

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:49.380
but it is in itself the climax of a Saga that
has started with Punk Hazard, with Kaido himself

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:54.900
being set up as a major player and antagonist
back on Thriller bark, which was released

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:56.830
in 2007.

00:02:56.830 --> 00:03:03.430
2007, that is a conflict in the making for
15 years.

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:07.870
And even though there was only very little
Eiichiro Oda the author of One PIece was willing

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:13.790
to share about him until we actually reached
Wano, it was as clear as Elon Musk's midlife

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:18.080
crisis that our rubbery hero would face off
against Kaido.

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:23.050
At the latest when he formed his pirate alliance
with Trafalgar Law on Punk Hazard to take

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:24.710
down the emperor.

00:03:24.710 --> 00:03:30.230
When we actually make it to Wano, Kaido has
been set up to be this invincible monster,

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:36.990
that not only is indestructible in battle,
but also is one of the politically most influential

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:40.130
players in the one piece world.

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:45.460
He deals weapons with the government, builds
an army of artificial devil fruit users, that

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:51.840
he produces himself across multiple islands
throughout the new world, and he rules over

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:59.020
an entire county, that is home to arguably
the most powerful group of people in the entire

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:00.020
story.

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:04.770
Not only that, but he also is also a former
member of the infamous Rocks pirates, that

00:04:04.770 --> 00:04:10.540
needed the pirate king Gol D Roger and the
hero of the marines Monkey D Garp to work

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:12.630
together to defeat.

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:18.239
Side by side with the likes of whitebeard,
Big Mom and Shiki and he is still trying to

00:04:18.239 --> 00:04:20.140
find the one piece himself.

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:25.740
In other words, when Luffy arrives at the
shores of Wano, I think it's fair to say that

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:31.960
in the big picture of things, Kaido is arguably
his biggest rival to becoming king of the

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:32.960
pirates.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:37.780
All right, so after seeing Kaido's dragon
form and all the misery he brings to the people

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:43.850
of this country, Luffy who just successfully
upgraded his observation haki to pro and defeated

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:51.180
the most powerful member of Big Mom's pirate
crew, of course has to face this man.

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:58.460
Only to get completely hammered into the ground,
by a Kaido that, and this is true, is also

00:04:58.460 --> 00:04:59.770
completely hammered.

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:04.690
Now, Luffy has been defeated by major villains
in the story before.

00:05:04.690 --> 00:05:11.030
Like by crocodile in alabasta or Moria, it's
a pretty common thing actually, showing us

00:05:11.030 --> 00:05:16.000
how luffy overcomes his own weaknesses and
takes down his opponent.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:22.620
However I would argue that the gap between
Luffy and Kaido at the beginning of wano is

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:26.760
far more gaping than the one crocodile left
him.

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:33.240
In other words, Luffy will have to grow immensely
to even stand a chance.

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:36.950
Which of course he does.

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:42.930
He learns Ryouu, grinding trait points and
finally unlocking armament haki on a completely

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:44.520
new level.

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:47.950
Kaido meanwhile has formed an alliance with
Big Mom, another Yonko.

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:49.570
But you know, no biggie.

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:56.180
And after raising Onigashima out of the ground,
a way better time bomb than the birdcage I

00:05:56.180 --> 00:06:02.860
think, the entire capital is at risk of being
crushed under a surprisingly aesthetic looking

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:03.890
giant skull.

00:06:03.890 --> 00:06:10.130
In other words, we suddenly have ended up
with the highest possible stakes for any 1v1

00:06:10.130 --> 00:06:16.120
battle luffy ever had, except Marineford with
Ace's life on the line of course, but then

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:21.380
again, that was not exactly the classic Luffy
vs the villain arc in the first place, so

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:22.710
it doesn't count.

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:26.580
The stakes are absolutely awesome.

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:32.240
With the scabbards, Yamato and all the other
supernova having failed to deal any major

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:38.639
damage to this gigantic blue dragon, Luffy
is the last man standing who has any hope

00:06:38.639 --> 00:06:43.310
of actually defeating him and somehow win
this war for the alliance.

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:48.120
At this point, the main motivation for Luffy
sailing to Onigashima to take down Kaido is

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:54.669
two-fold: Freeing Wano from his tyranny, while
at the same time taking out his biggest rival

00:06:54.669 --> 00:06:57.350
and gate-keeper to reaching laugh tale.

00:06:57.350 --> 00:07:03.790
Or from a storytelling perspective, legitimising
Luffy as one of the emperors and playing on

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:10.340
the highest power level of the story in preparation
for other big shots like Akainu or Blackbeard.

00:07:10.340 --> 00:07:16.430
Now, since you already know what's gonna happen,
no need to follow the line of events here.

00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:20.380
Because there is actually another motivation
added to the mix as well.

00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:26.050
As it looks like Kaido was actively trying
to bring about the return of joy boy and change

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:31.330
the world, as I explained in more detail his
character analysis, it will be Luffy's job

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:36.729
to free Kaido from this self-induced state
of suffering, where he feels like he is the

00:07:36.729 --> 00:07:41.290
only one who can change anything and so he
has to do it, even if there is collateral

00:07:41.290 --> 00:07:43.460
damage and he has to play the villain.

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:49.520
Once again, mixing his fights with Katakuri,
Crocodile and Dofi, it's about Luffy not only

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:55.979
freeing the country and the princess, but
also about freeing the villain himself.

00:07:55.979 --> 00:08:00.871
In other words, I feel like Oda took the best
parts out of each of Luffy's previous best

00:08:00.871 --> 00:08:06.930
fights and mashed them into a soup of peak
storytelling awesomeness here, like mixing

00:08:06.930 --> 00:08:13.490
the best alcohol, gin, the best plant, rosemary
and the best water, tonic, into the ultimate

00:08:13.490 --> 00:08:14.490
beverage.

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:15.490
Perfection.

00:08:15.490 --> 00:08:20.259
And lucky me, I accidentally built myself
the perfect bridge into talking about how

00:08:20.259 --> 00:08:23.270
Luffy and Kaido have grown throughout this
fight.

00:08:23.270 --> 00:08:29.320
Luffy once again cements his determination
to become king of the pirates or die trying,

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:33.039
his change is much more physical.

00:08:33.039 --> 00:08:38.529
After failing to have any major impact on
Kaido even with his newfound ultra fancy shockwave

00:08:38.529 --> 00:08:45.300
flowing armament haki, he follows Rayleigh's
advice and lets his Haki bloom.

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:50.769
He learns to use his conquorors haki as a
weapon, which is more effective, but still

00:08:50.769 --> 00:08:52.779
not enough.

00:08:52.779 --> 00:08:58.209
Kaido keeps almost knocking him out to the
point where Luffy actually loses his life

00:08:58.209 --> 00:08:59.639
for a second.

00:08:59.639 --> 00:09:08.559
It is at this point, where we get the biggest
reveal of the story yet with Luffy's awakening

00:09:08.559 --> 00:09:12.519
of his mythical zoan devil fruit and of JoyBoy
himself.

00:09:12.519 --> 00:09:18.449
By the way both these power-ups, the conquerors
haki and the devil fruit reveal have been

00:09:18.449 --> 00:09:23.850
wonderfully worked towards for many chapters
during the raid on onigashima.

00:09:23.850 --> 00:09:31.379
In other words, Luffy is learning how to be
a Yonko in this fight.

00:09:31.379 --> 00:09:36.490
BUT EVEN STILL, it's not enough to actually
take down Kaido.

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:43.209
He has closed the gap between them dramatically,
but despite awakening one of the most powerful

00:09:43.209 --> 00:09:49.970
devil fruits, I mean maybe even THE strongest,
the emperor still has no problem keeping up

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:51.019
with Luffy.

00:09:51.019 --> 00:09:55.450
But the playing field has been levelled.

00:09:55.450 --> 00:10:02.100
That's JUST for Luffy, who I think also has
some of his best moments in the entire series.

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:04.860
Walking between big mom and Kaido.

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:07.449
Revealing Gear 5 and becoming a giant.

00:10:07.449 --> 00:10:11.889
Riding Momo.

00:10:11.889 --> 00:10:17.439
And sending Zoro, Law and Kid down so he can
deal with Kaido himself.

00:10:17.439 --> 00:10:21.189
Kaido's arc meanwhile is completely character
focused.

00:10:21.189 --> 00:10:26.679
Again, if you want the whole story, I recommend
you check out my video on that, but in summary:

00:10:26.679 --> 00:10:33.089
He goes from a nihilistic and depressed drunk
at the beginning of wano, that is disappointed

00:10:33.089 --> 00:10:39.730
by Luffy's abilities to smiling, acknowledging
Luffy's growth and genuinely enjoying this

00:10:39.730 --> 00:10:40.730
fight.

00:10:40.730 --> 00:10:46.259
And again, I think having Kaido laugh as he
used to in the past and become his old self

00:10:46.259 --> 00:10:49.990
again, is a major part of this.

00:10:49.990 --> 00:10:56.360
To me, he has quickly developed from a club-swinging
evil brute, to one of the most complex, emotionally

00:10:56.360 --> 00:11:00.850
expressive and genuinely interesting antagonists.

00:11:00.850 --> 00:11:05.869
During this fight the characters involved
and also myself have basically gone through

00:11:05.869 --> 00:11:07.879
any emotion imaginable.

00:11:07.879 --> 00:11:13.939
Hype, anger, fear, happiness, sadness, shock.

00:11:13.939 --> 00:11:20.180
It's been a true whirlwind of feelings and
thoughts for me ever since chapter 1000.

00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:25.790
Then of course we have the artwork and choreography.

00:11:25.790 --> 00:11:27.899
And what can I say.

00:11:27.899 --> 00:11:35.189
There has just NOTHING like it ever been in
the story of one piece before.

00:11:35.189 --> 00:11:41.829
Kaido's design in all of his form is just
absolutely breathtaking.

00:11:41.829 --> 00:11:47.040
One Piece isn't exactly famous for it's fight
scenes, but the movements and attacks throughout

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:53.630
all are drawn in such a dynamic and energetic
way that it captured me much more than many

00:11:53.630 --> 00:11:55.459
of the previous fights.

00:11:55.459 --> 00:12:01.259
Oda-sensei truly made me feel the impact and
power behind every single punch.

00:12:01.259 --> 00:12:09.009
There is a great balance between dialogue
and action, between humour and seriousness

00:12:09.009 --> 00:12:15.600
and most importantly between giving us a new
perspective on the fight and letting things

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:18.000
play out for a while.

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:23.589
A true masterpiece of storytelling and fighting
choreography, that has made me fall in love

00:12:23.589 --> 00:12:28.410
and relish in the greatness of this story
more than ever and that I think will be tough

00:12:28.410 --> 00:12:30.309
to top in the future.

00:12:30.309 --> 00:12:34.850
However, if you truly want to take this to
the next level and understand the depth and

